From 1ab2c6aa1b1f428f2410f340e21a33944308f1be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:13:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] chore: lock the drift-gate + guest-room inputs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

flake.nix has declared `drift-gate` and `guest-room` since the
descriptor-honesty edge landed (#29), but flake.lock never gained entries
for them, so every `nix flake check` / status build silently locked them
at whatever upstream HEAD was that day. With contract-check now a
blocking gate that would make its result depend on unpinned repos — pin
them like every other input (descriptor-honesty passes at these revs).

Entries computed the same validated way as the re-pin commit; `nix flake
lock` regenerates them identically.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CVjvRP7P9oSiX3uhjK1xsz
---
 flake.lock | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)

